---
code: wrapper-entry-incoherent
when-fires: a wrapper's `__enter` and `__lend_map` disagree on argv flow. oracle/validate.rs peel_and_entry_coherence. Spanned (the entry name_span).
why: 27C:rul-fold-entry-coherence-failfast (declarations-genuinely-contradict): a pre-network fail-fast. The holes are typed: `{wrapper}` plus the two disagreeing depths.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# The fold reads two leading arguments off the front; the entry form reads one, so the guest the
# entry hands the tool starts at a different token than the fold measured.
runas__lend_map() {
   shift 2
   printf '%s\n' root : lends user
   : lends fs-view
   : lends netns
   "$@"
}

runas__enter() {
   shift
   runas -n "$@"
}

